lg:AT-DSB-2021-D155027-spruch-2-q1-en
    a lgo:Translation ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:Draft ;
    lgo:sourceTextSha256 "2e222b93aa4b3f097553b009612401aff8fa2cc73c6ae74c9649b2805cfc2384" ;
    lgo:text """2. The complaint against the first respondent is upheld, and it is found that
a) the first respondent, as controller, by implementing the tool “Google Analytics” on its website at www.xyz.at, transferred personal data of the complainant (at least unique user identification numbers, IP address and browser parameters) to the second respondent at least on 14 August 2020,
b) the standard data protection clauses which the first respondent concluded with the second respondent do not offer an adequate level of protection under Article 44 GDPR, because
i) the second respondent is to be qualified as a provider of electronic communication services within the meaning of 50 U.S. Code § 1881(b)(4) and as such is subject to surveillance by US intelligence services under 50 U.S. Code § 1881a (“FISA 702”), and
ii) the measures taken in addition to the standard data protection clauses referred to in point 2.b) are not effective, since they do not eliminate the possibilities of surveillance and access by US intelligence services,
c) in the present case, no other instrument under Chapter V of the GDPR can be relied on for the data transfer referred to in point 2.a), and the first respondent therefore did not ensure an adequate level of protection under Article 44 GDPR for the data transfer referred to in point 2.a)."""@en ;
    lgo:translatedBy "claude-opus-5-5" ;
    lgo:translatedOn "2026-11-04"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:translationMethod lgv:MachineTranslation ;
    lgo:translationOf lg:AT-DSB-2021-D155027-spruch-2-q1 .

